1. Software derived from llama.cpp / ggml (MIT)
===============================================================================

hipml includes logic translated from llama.cpp and ggml
(https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), Copyright (c) the ggml authors,
used under the MIT License (the full text is in docs/reference/LICENSE).

Ported logic, and the file that carries it:

  the qwen3next / qwen3_5 hybrid architecture math (llama.cpp's
  src/models/qwen35.cpp and llama-graph.cpp)
      crates/hipml-model/src/gpu.rs            layer loop, attention block,
                                               gated-delta-net block, FFN

  gated delta net and the recurrent state
      crates/hipml-core/src/delta.rs           ggml_compute_forward_ssm_conv_f32,
                                               build_delta_net_autoregressive,
                                               fused-kernel semantics from
                                               gated_delta_net_f32.c
      crates/hipml-kernels/kernels/ssm_conv1d_f32.hip
      crates/hipml-kernels/kernels/ssm_gates_f32.hip
                                               ggml_compute_softplus_f32 branch

  rms_norm, rope and MROPE
      crates/hipml-core/src/ops.rs             ggml_rms_norm identity,
                                               ggml_compute_forward_rope_flt,
                                               ggml_mrope_cache_init
      crates/hipml-kernels/kernels/mrope_f32.hip
                                               GGML_ROPE_TYPE_MROPE semantics

  quantized block formats
      crates/hipml-core/src/quant.rs           dequantize_row_q5_K and the
                                               GGML block layouts
      crates/hipml-core/src/kv.rs              q8_0 / q4_0 block layout and
                                               scale convention
      crates/hipml-kernels/kernels/kv_encode.hip
      crates/hipml-kernels/kernels/gemv_q4_k.hip
      crates/hipml-kernels/kernels/gemv_q5_k.hip
      crates/hipml-kernels/kernels/gemv_q6_k.hip
      crates/hipml-kernels/kernels/gemv_q8_0.hip
      crates/hipml-kernels/kernels/dequant_q4_k_f32.hip
      crates/hipml-kernels/kernels/prefill_q4_k.hip
      crates/hipml-kernels/kernels/prefill_q6_k.hip
      crates/hipml-kernels/kernels/prefill_q8_0.hip
                                               block format decoding follows
                                               ggml's layout; the kernels
                                               themselves are original

  tokenizer: the pretokenizer split pattern, BPE and the byte encoder
      crates/hipml-core/src/tokenizer.rs       from llama-vocab.cpp and
                                               unicode.cpp
      crates/hipml-core/src/unicode_tables.rs  generated from src/unicode-data.cpp
      bench/tokenizer/gen_unicode_table.py     the generator for that table

  chat template rendering
      crates/hipml-core/src/chat.rs            tool | tojson rendering, matching
                                               llama.cpp's template engine

Each of those files says so in its header. Nothing above is copied verbatim;
it is a translation whose inputs are the reference copies in docs/reference/.

Upstream revision. The reference copies in docs/reference/ are from llama.cpp
tag b12126 (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/tree/b12126), and the port was
audited against that tag. The Unicode tables are generated from llama.cpp
commit d7725699 (src/unicode-data.cpp). The benchmark baseline is llama.cpp
build 11820, commit d7725699. Where a file names a different revision, that
file's header wins.

