2. Reference copies in docs/reference/ (MIT, documentation only)
===============================================================================

docs/reference/ holds eleven unmodified llama.cpp source files:

    qwen35.cpp              delta-net-base.cpp      gated_delta_net_f32.c
    models.h                llama-graph.cpp         llama-vocab.cpp
    unicode.cpp             unicode.h               ggml-cpu-ops.cpp
    ggml-quants.c           ggml-impl.h

They are Copyright (c) the ggml authors, licensed under the MIT License; the
full text is docs/reference/LICENSE, and docs/reference/README.md says which
file is used for what. They are kept so the port can be audited line by line,
exactly as upstream published them, so their bytes - including line numbers
cited in docs/notes/ - are unchanged. They are documentation only: nothing in
docs/reference/ is compiled, linked or shipped in a build, and they are not
covered by hipml's Apache-2.0 license.

docs/reference/ggml-cpu-ops.cpp contains YaRN code that carries its own notice:
"MIT licensed. Copyright (c) 2023 Jeffrey Quesnelle and Bowen Peng."

